# 24. INTERACTION DESIGN

The website should reward exploration.

Use:

- hover effects
- scroll-based transitions
- line drawing
- node highlighting
- subtle cursor interaction
- progressive reveal
- text distortion
- signal pulses

But maintain performance.

Animations must not cause:

- excessive CPU usage
- layout shifts
- unusable mobile experience
- inaccessible navigation

Respect reduced-motion preferences.

---

# 25. RESPONSIVE DESIGN

Must work properly on:

- desktop
- laptop
- tablet
- mobile

On mobile:

- simplify constellation visualization
- preserve storytelling
- preserve character identity
- preserve navigation
- reduce decorative animations

Never simply shrink desktop UI.

Design mobile intentionally.

---

# 26. ACCESSIBILITY

Implement:

- semantic HTML
- keyboard navigation
- visible focus states
- readable contrast
- alt text where appropriate
- reduced-motion support
- accessible buttons
- accessible navigation

Decorative animations must not prevent interaction.

---

# 27. TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION

FIRST inspect the existing repository.

Determine:

- framework
- routing
- package manager
- component architecture
- styling system
- existing design tokens
- existing assets
- existing animation system
- existing reusable components

DO NOT unnecessarily replace the existing stack.

Reuse existing infrastructure whenever possible.

If the project already uses:

- React
- Next.js
- Vite
- Tailwind
- shadcn/ui

follow the existing architecture and conventions.

---

# 28. COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE

Create reusable components.

Suggested structure:

